s/DcaShop.E2eTests/Pages/ProductCatalogPage.cs:61-62` finds the \"Our Products\" heading by its HTML role, because the heading has no `data-test` attribute. `project/product.md` says every element a test addresses carries a stable `data-test` attribute, and no other page object finds elements this way.\n- **Suggested fix:** add `data-test=\"catalog-heading\"` to the heading at `Catalog.cshtml:8` and read it through a `data-test` selector. The Java template needs the same attribute, since the views mirror it one to one.\n- **Alternative:** drop the heading check from the browser test. `ProductPageTest.cs:69-70` already asserts \"Our Products\", but this would depart from the plan.\n\n**Not checked:**\n- **Scenario sync (possible issue, not a finding):** the new test's display name has to appear as a scenario title in `../dca-sample-specification/scenarios.md` and in the Java suite. The Java template may also still say \"Products\". I didn't read either repository because they're outside this stage's inputs, so this still needs confirming before the story is accepted. It only fails when the tests run with `-p:SpecificationPath`.\n- **DCA review not run:** the extra `dca` review the profile adds was not run. The diff contains no domain, port or adapter code, but the report says plainly that this review is missing.\n- **Review skills not loaded:** the ddd, hexagonal and clean-code reviews ran in this session from the stage's own descriptions. I didn't load the project's review skills for them, to stay within the stage's inputs.\n\nI changed no code and ran no other stage.","ttft_ms":3036,"type":"result","duration_ms":79845,"uuid":"21c08b7e-9189-4d70-bc47-6d78fb3450ff","ttft_stream_ms":1805,"time_to_request_ms":38,"first_content_frame_ms":1806,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
